{"schema":2,"id":"KH0219","investigatorId":"AS201","provenance":"Ica","discoveredBy":null,"discoveredOn":null,"collection":{"name":"Phoebe A. Hearst Museum of Anthropology","city":"Berkeley, CA","country":"USA"},"notes":"1. AS201, 202, and 203 are designated by the same museum number. They are similar in color. Five colors are used; one is on all three of the quipus and another is on two of the three. All have groups consistent by color patterning. The values on them are the same order of magnitude. All values are 0-20. All group sums are below 40. (See AS202 Observation 4 for other materials found with these quipus.) 2. AS201, 202, 203, and 204 are all designated by the museum as TK. This collection is discussed in D. Menzel in \"Pottery Style and Society in Ancient Peru\", Berkeley and Los Angeles, University of California Press 1976. Its provenance is Ica. 3. By spacing, the quipu is separated into three groups of 2, 4, 4 pendants. Both pendants in the first group are color B. Each pendant in the next two groups is color LB with one subsidiary. The subsidiaries in the first of these two groups are LB. E","primaryCord":{"length":17.5,"color":"B","beginning":"T","termination":"K","notes":""},"cords":[{"parent":null,"level":1,"up":false,"position":2.0,"positionRecorded":true,"length":21,"color":"B","colorOperator":null,"color2":null,"termination":"B","twist":null,"attachment":null,"fiber":null,"group":1,"knots":[{"position":6,"type":"S","count":1,"value":10,"direction":null},{"position":13.5,"type":"L","count":1,"value":4,"direction":null}],"note":""},{"parent":null,"level":1,"up":false,"position":2.5,"positionRecorded":true,"length":33.5,"color":"B","colorOperator":null,"color2":null,"termination":"K","twist":null,"attachment":null,"fiber":null,"group":1,"knots":[{"position":6.5,"type":"S","count":1,"value":10,"direction":null},{"position":13.5,"type":"L","count":1,"value":7,"direction":null}],"note":""},{"parent":null,"level":1,"up":false,"position":4.5,"positionR